Subject: [PATCH] websocket: keep parsing frames already buffered after a fragment

WebSocketConnectionImpl::onNewMessage returns as soon as a parsed frame does
not complete a message, so the next fragments of that message, already in
the buffer, wait until more bytes arrive on the connection. A client that
fragments a message and then waits for the answer (an ESP-IDF websocket
client splits any message larger than its buffer, e.g. a Sleep Bridge's
hello) never gets one. Keep parsing while whole frames are consumed; return
only when the frame at the head of the buffer is incomplete.

Against drogon v1.9.0 (Debian trixie's libdrogon 1.9.0+ds); applies to
v1.9.13 unchanged. Upstream v1.9.14 and master still have the early return.

--- a/lib/src/WebSocketConnectionImpl.cc
+++ b/lib/src/WebSocketConnectionImpl.cc
@@ -384,12 +384,22 @@
     auto self = shared_from_this();
     while (buffer->readableBytes() > 0)
     {
+        const size_t before = buffer->readableBytes();
         auto success = parser_.parse(buffer);
         if (success)
         {
             std::string message;
             WebSocketMessageType type;
-            if (parser_.gotAll(message, type))
+            if (!parser_.gotAll(message, type))
+            {
+                // A whole frame that is not the message's last (a fragment)
+                // was consumed: the next frames may already be buffered, so
+                // keep parsing. Return only when the frame is incomplete
+                // (nothing consumed) and more bytes must arrive first.
+                if (buffer->readableBytes() < before)
+                    continue;
+                return;
+            }
             {
                 if (type == WebSocketMessageType::Ping)
                 {
@@ -409,10 +419,6 @@
                 //           << "\n(type=" << (int)type << ")";
                 messageCallback_(std::move(message), self, type);
             }
-            else
-            {
-                return;
-            }
         }
         else
         {
